  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Energy and Self-Reliance Programme (ENSER) - Energy Component</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The Multi-Donor Action `Energy and Self-Reliance Programme (ENSER)&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;&#xbf;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(192, 0, 0);&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;is jointly co-financed by the European Union and the Federal Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development (BMZ)&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(227, 108, 10);&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;and implemented by GIZ as part of &lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;the BMZ project `Promotion of Renewa&lt;/span&gt;ble Energy and Energy Efficiency Programme&#xbf; (PREEEP). The total budget of this Action is 14,000,000 EUR (EU contribution 10,000,000 EUR and BMZ contribution 4,000,000 EUR).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Action aims to improve &lt;strong&gt;EN&lt;/strong&gt;ergy access and &lt;strong&gt;Se&lt;/strong&gt;lf-&lt;strong&gt;R&lt;/strong&gt;eliance (EN SER) in displacement settings and will be implemented in an integrated manner by GIZ PREEEP being awarded the energy related ENSER Action (this contribution agreement) and the World Food Programme (WFP) being awarded the Self-Reliance ENSER Action.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Overall Objective&lt;/strong&gt; of the Action is to address forced displacement (asylum seekers, refugees, refugee returnees and IDPs) in selected Sub-Saharan African countries through regional approaches.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Specific Objective&lt;/strong&gt; (outcome) of the Action is: To improve the access of forcibly displaced populations, in particular women, persons with disabilities and children, and host/resident communities to effective basic services, accessible housing and economic inclusion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This ambition will be reached through the following five interlinked areas of support: (1) Strengthened competencies of professionals and managers of selected public organisations for the implementation of strategies for market development, decentralisation and/or gender equality in the renewable energy and energy efficiency sectors; (2) Public and private actors are fulfilling their role as drivers of market development for renewable energy and energy efficiency in Uganda; (3) Enhanced processes by district administrations to incorporate sustainable energy solutions into their budget and strategic planning; (4) Public, private and civil society players have actively contributed to the sustainable organisation of the energy sector; (5) Digital applications that promote the productive use of electricity have been introduced in micro, small and medium-sized enterprises and civil society organisations in refugee settlements and host communities.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
